{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "integral_lev_cumulative_from_bottom",
    "description": "Cumulative integral from the SURFACE to the centre of the current layer: lowers integral(f, var: lev, lower: a, upper: lev) -- the upper bound literally the axis name, esm-spec 4.2 'partial/cumulative' mode -- to the layer field F[k] = sum_{j<k} f[j] dz[j] + f[k] dz[k]/2, i.e. the midpoint-rule integral from ze[1] to zc[k] (the whole layers below plus half of the current layer). Priority 10 over the whole-column form. F[1] = f[1] dz[1]/2 (the empty prefix sum is zero). The integrand `f` must be a bare layer-shaped (lev) field of THIS grid (where {f: {shape: [lev]}}, esm-spec 9.6.1); bind a compound integrand to a declared [lev] observed first. The measure is the consumer's free-name layer-thickness observed `dz` (grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm) -- rebind it at the import edge (esm-spec 9.7.7) to integrate against another monotone layer measure such as dp/g. The integral node's `var` names the axis (`lev`); esm-spec 4.2 leaves the bounds measure-free, so the bounds carry no numeric weight here: they select the FORM of the sum (whole column / cumulative from the surface / cumulative from the top / to layer centres / to interfaces) and are otherwise documentation. Because the layer values are midpoint samples, every form is the composite midpoint rule and is second-order accurate on a smoothly stretched column.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:column_nonuniform_1d",
      "op:integral",
      "order:2",
      "stencil_width:1",
      "bc:none",
      "spec:9.6.8",
      "axes:lev"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.13 (nonuniform grids)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Davis, P. J. and Rabinowitz, P. (1984). Methods of Numerical Integration, 2nd ed. Academic Press. Section 2.1 (the midpoint rule and its error)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "integral_lev_cumulative_from_bottom": {
      "params": [
        "f",
        "a"
      ],
      "priority": 10,
      "match": {
        "op": "integral",
        "args": [
          "f"
        ],
        "var": "lev",
        "lower": "a",
        "upper": "lev"
      },
      "where": {
        "f": {
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ]
        }
      },
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "k"
            ],
            "reduce": "+",
            "args": [
              "f"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "k": {
                "from": "lev"
              },
              "j": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "filter": {
              "op": "<",
              "args": [
                "j",
                "k"
              ]
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "f",
                    "j"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "dz",
                    "j"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              0.5,
              "f",
              "dz"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
